When I save a game, it prints dots (".") for each level it writes to the 
disk (presumably so that those with slow drives can tell that something 
is happening).  However, it starts around the 50th column.  If you're deep
enough it passes beyond the 80th column.  Then, errors like:
"bad win 3 cursor position (map window): (81,1)" and so on.
(this isn't a fatal error, just annoying...)  A simple check to 
wrap around might take a whole line or two.... ;-)

Also, when I was in Gehennum, and prayed to Crom (after converting the altar
from Moloch), it said something about Crom not being able to help me.  Then
Moloch said something evil sounding, and it gave the (standard?)
"``Then die, mortal!''  unaligned character?" error message.  This
was mentioned before by someone.

I am playing the pre-standard distribution that was posted on wuarchive
last week.  The bugs were reproducible on the standard version (which *must*
have been compiled with Microsoft C; it's inexcusably slow, even on my
486/50!).


